@startuml
' purpose: approved OpenCode-only host-owned OAuth policy and its implementation gates
' covers: defs/opencode/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/opencode/README.md
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime
' covers: packages/lib/opencode-credentials.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_credentials.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_runtime.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_runtime_native.py
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/sbx/secret.go
' covers: e2e/opencode_credentials_test.go
' covers: e2e/opencode_auth_test.go
' status: PLANNED; Executor selected host-owned OAuth on 2026-10-09.
' Implementation remains unapproved and unshipped; this change documents the policy only.
' Scope: the OpenCode harness family, including its browser image; other harnesses remain unchanged.
' Existing boundary: _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
' Existing implementation: _spec/defs/opencode/native-v2-integration.puml
' Startup evidence: _spec/packages/lib/opencode-seed-progress.puml
' Storage redesign: _spec/_plans/opencode-versioned-history-storage.puml
' Official storage/precedence: https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/cli/providers
' Host credential model: https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/credentials/
' OpenCode sandbox setup: https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/agents/opencode/
'
' CURRENT: V2 persists provider credentials in SQLite, not new auth.json writes.
' Snapshot publication deletes credential/account/control_account tokens and clears account_state.
' Session history, permissions and artifacts survive; saved in-sandbox logins do not.
' PROVEO_KEEP_AGENT_LOGINS controls filename denial, not SQLite token publication.
' Observed current sandbox: SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=apikey; OPENAI_API_KEY holds a sentinel.
' Logs show credential creation in one native run and an API-key failure in the following run.
' This observation does not establish the host proxy's secret contents or substitution behavior.
'
' PLANNED selection has three explicit modes: host-owned-oauth, ephemeral-oauth, api-key.
' These are policy identifiers, not current CLI flags or implemented configuration fields.
' Persist the selected mode and nonsecret account identity independently of session snapshots.
' Host-owned OAuth is the selected persistence target; ephemeral OAuth remains an explicit option.
' API-key mode requires separate consent because it can use metered billing rather than a subscription.
' Never reinterpret a missing OAuth connection as permission to use an API key or proxy sentinel.
'
' Host storage keeps access/refresh tokens and expiry in an OS keychain or host-private store.
' Keep every token store outside all sandbox mounts, including the shared proveo-home tree.
' Refresh and serialize token rotation on the host; reconnect explicitly after revocation or refresh failure.
' A credential reference identifies one provider/account/method without containing a usable secret.
' Per-run account wiring must select OpenCode's OAuth connector/method and subscription endpoint.
' OPENAI_API_KEY alone does not encode a native ChatGPT subscription connection.
'
' IMPLEMENTATION GATES: determine how the pinned V2 connector accepts a host-brokered account.
' Verify endpoint, headers, account metadata, transport and refresh with the actual pinned CLI.
' Do not assume sbx's API-key injection route provides OpenCode's ChatGPT OAuth integration.
' Keep refresh tokens host-only; never bypass the snapshot sanitizer or broaden KEEP_AGENT_LOGINS.
' If safe account brokering is unsupported, stop with an actionable unsupported-policy/reconnect message.
' Do not silently expose raw tokens to the guest as an alternative implementation.
'
' ACCEPTANCE: separate actual OpenCode runs retain the selected OAuth account without reconnecting.
' Both runs use the subscription endpoint; neither sends a literal proxy sentinel upstream.
' Forced expiry refreshes once on the host; revocation produces reconnect guidance without API fallback.
' Teardown, recovery, logs and durable snapshots contain no access/refresh tokens.
' Concurrent runs cannot corrupt token rotation or cross-select another account.
' Existing API-key mode and credential-free session resume retain their behavior.
' These live OAuth gates remain pending; current tests verify the existing sanitizer only.
' FK (manual syllables): POLICY 11.2 (29w/52s); STORE 11.5 (25w/47s); ACCOUNT 11.4 (31w/55s).
'
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title PLANNED — OpenCode-only host-owned OAuth persistence
left to right direction

actor "Executor\nexplicit authentication choice" as OP
component "OpenCode policy selection\nPLANNED: persisted nonsecret mode\nprovider + account + method" as POLICY <<app>>
database "Host-owned OAuth store\nPLANNED: outside every guest mount" as STORE <<db>>
component "Host OAuth broker\nPLANNED: refresh + account routing" as BROKER <<host>>
component "Pinned OpenCode V2 connector\nPLANNED: explicit per-run OAuth account" as ACCOUNT <<app>>
component "packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime\nCURRENT: private per-run database" as RUNTIME <<app>>
component "packages/lib/opencode-credentials.py\nCURRENT: credential-free publication" as SCRUB <<app>>
database "OpenCode durable history\nsessions + artifacts; no saved tokens" as HISTORY <<db>>
component "ChatGPT subscription endpoint\nPLANNED: OAuth route, not API-key fallback" as VENDOR <<cloud>>
component "Reconnect required\nPLANNED: missing, expired or unsupported auth" as RECONNECT <<error>>

OP --> POLICY : select host-owned OAuth
POLICY --> STORE : resolve account reference
STORE --> BROKER : host-only tokens
BROKER --> ACCOUNT : account binding; protocol gate pending
ACCOUNT --> RUNTIME : per-run connection
RUNTIME --> BROKER : authenticated subscription request
BROKER --> VENDOR : inject + refresh on approved route
RUNTIME --> SCRUB : preserve existing boundary
SCRUB --> HISTORY : publish session state without tokens
POLICY --> RECONNECT : no usable OAuth connection

note bottom of POLICY
  Save the chosen login mode apart from account
  tokens so a missing login cannot change the
  billing route. Require consent before treating
  an environment sentinel as an API-key
  connection.
end note

note bottom of STORE
  Store tokens on the host outside every guest
  mount, including shared history folders.
  Remove credentials from saved session snapshots
  on exit and during interrupted-run recovery.
end note

note bottom of ACCOUNT
  Test the account binding with the pinned native
  connector before enabling subscription access.
  If the proxy cannot provide that binding,
  reject the policy instead of forwarding tokens
  or switching billing modes.
end note
@enduml
